# Sample 11 — Indicative scale
#
# Criteria four orders of magnitude apart (200 A vs 45 kA) would
# either crush the small end on a linear axis or force a log axis
# whether or not that reads well for the audience. `scale indicative`
# instead orders every value with even, non-calibrated spacing and
# labels itself clearly as not-to-scale.

diagram "Indicative overview" {
  scale indicative
  range auto

  below "Secondary CT saturation limit" must 200 A
  above "Maximum fault at remote busbar" must 45 kA margin 10%

  selected "Setting" 8 kA
}
